# Driving the Minecraft Server

## Player sidekick

Players use only `/agent <prompt>` in Minecraft chat. The Paper plugin opens an
authenticated outbound WebSocket to `mc-agent`; the Python runtime routes typed
actions back to native Bukkit/FAWE executors.

- Do not add MCP, external AI-control APIs, model-visible console commands, or
  RCON dispatch to the sidekick.
- Deterministic Tier S/A routes must run before the local model.
- The plugin revalidates permissions, GriefPrevention claims, deadlines, edit
  budgets, and idempotency for every mutation.
- Builds must be verified and undoable. Never teleport a player to paste or
  load a build.
- Bedrock names retain their leading Floodgate dot.

Canonical contracts live in `protocol/`; runtime code lives in `companion/`;
native executors live in `plugins/neighborhood-agent/`; declarative skills live
in `skills/`.

## Host operations

For operator terminal work use:

- `./mc.sh status | list | logs | console | backup`
- `./mc.sh op <name>` / `./mc.sh deop <name>`
- `./mc.sh say "<message>"`
- `./mc.sh gamemode <mode> <player>`
- `./mc.sh cmd "<explicit command>"` only as an operator escape hatch
- `make companion-gate` for the locked accuracy/latency suite
- `make companion-deploy` to build and deploy runtime + plugin

Raw `docker exec ... rcon-cli` is a last resort. Before destructive world
operations, restate coordinates and approximate block count, then back up.
